cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use nbpearson in research, cite the software and identify the exact
  version used. Cite a version-specific archived DOI when one is available.
type: software
title: "nbpearson: explicit negative-binomial Pearson-residual linear operators"
version: 0.1.0.dev1
authors:
  - family-names: Kone
    given-names: Mohamed
abstract: >-
  Python CPU/binary64 linear operators with explicitly selected interpolated,
  interpolated-grouped and exact-grouped representations for centered,
  optionally clipped, fixed negative-binomial Pearson residuals of sparse
  integer counts. The original nbpearson software is MIT-licensed.
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/mohkone/nbpearson"
keywords:
  - sparse counts
  - Pearson residuals
  - negative binomial
  - linear operators
